{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":996,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"Moreover the LORD answered Job,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3189},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":997,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"“Shall he who argues contend with the Almighty? He who argues with God, let him answer it.”","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3191},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":998,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"Then Job answered the LORD,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3195},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":999,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"“Behold, I am of small account. What will I answer you? I lay my hand on my mouth.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3197},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1000,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"I have spoken once, and I will not answer; Yes, twice, but I will proceed no further.”","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3200},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1001,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind:","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3204},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1002,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"“Now brace yourself like a man. I will question you, and you will answer me.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3206},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1003,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"Will you even annul my judgment? Will you condemn me, that you may be justified?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3209},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1004,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"Or do you have an arm like God? Can you thunder with a voice like him?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3212},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1005,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"“Now deck yourself with excellency and dignity. Array yourself with honor and majesty.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3216},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1006,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"Pour out the fury of your anger. Look at everyone who is proud, and bring him low.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3219},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1007,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"Look at everyone who is proud, and humble him. Crush the wicked in their place.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3222},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1008,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"Hide them in the dust together. Bind their faces in the hidden place.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3225},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1009,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"Then I will also admit to you that your own right hand can save you.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3228},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1010,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"“See now behemoth, which I made as well as you. He eats grass as an ox.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3232},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1011,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"Look now, his strength is in his thighs. His force is in the muscles of his belly.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3235},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1012,"verse_start":17,"verse_end":17,"verse_label":"17","text":"He moves his tail like a cedar. The sinews of his thighs are knit together.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3238},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1013,"verse_start":18,"verse_end":18,"verse_label":"18","text":"His bones are like tubes of bronze. His limbs are like bars of iron.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3241},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1014,"verse_start":19,"verse_end":19,"verse_label":"19","text":"He is the chief of the ways of God. He who made him gives him his sword.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3245},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1015,"verse_start":20,"verse_end":20,"verse_label":"20","text":"Surely the mountains produce food for him, where all the animals of the field play.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3248},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1016,"verse_start":21,"verse_end":21,"verse_label":"21","text":"He lies under the lotus trees, in the covert of the reed, and the marsh.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3251},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1017,"verse_start":22,"verse_end":22,"verse_label":"22","text":"The lotuses cover him with their shade. The willows of the brook surround him.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3254},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1018,"verse_start":23,"verse_end":23,"verse_label":"23","text":"Behold, if a river overflows, he doesn’t tremble. He is confident, though the Jordan swells even to his mouth.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3257},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":40,"verse_ordinal":1019,"verse_start":24,"verse_end":24,"verse_label":"24","text":"Shall any take him when he is on the watch, or pierce through his nose with a snare?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3260}]}